but luckily, you can just ask the model to teach you what you don't know", "createdAt": "2026-10-08T02:26:45.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/trq212/status/2108021248966135891", "likes": 148, "retweets": 7, "replies": 21, "isQuote": false, "quotedTweetId": null}, {"id": "2108021247301062894", "text": "the most common failure case I see is when people are working outside their domain of expertise and don't know how to be precise with their prompts and plans, so they have to spend a lot of turns iterating imprecisely https://t.co/mRT3knojCP", "createdAt": "2026-10-08T02:26:45.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/trq212/status/2108021247301062894", "likes": 1296, "retweets": 41, "replies": 86, "isQuote": true, "quotedTweetId": "2107959902174142725"}, {"id": "2107957206327173484", "text": "I think it's probably an incredible time to be a game dev content creator, for many people making games is a form of having fun and they're willing to pay for it! https://t.co/iS08bGZZnJ", "createdAt": "2026-10-07T22:12:16.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/trq212/status/2107957206327173484", "likes": 453, "retweets": 17, "replies": 44, "isQuote": true, "quotedTweetId": "2107879332609667481"}]}, "tweets": [{"id": "2108021248966135891", "text": "and because agents make it easier, almost everyone is operating outside their expertise at some point

